From 19b820b48f134541ec1455b3c7313394d80de788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:38:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] replica-freshness alarm: resume the awake clock
 across gateway restarts

The replica-freshness check (#2345) kept `(stamp, monotonic since, open)` per board only in process memory, and the
first observation after a start set `since = now`. hermes-hub restarts its gateway on every core update: 148 times
on 2026-11-13 UTC, median 4.2 min apart, and every telemetry line since deploy read `not advanced for 0 awake s`.
A replica stuck behind across restarts (the 2026-11-12 hub incident shape) therefore never reached
REPLICA_STALE_S = 1200 s and never alarmed; after a restart an open incident also re-filed (a comment via the
idempotent report path).

Fix: each observation is also written to `<kanban home>/kanban/.replica-age.json` (beside `.sync-state.json`) as
`{stamp, since, open, seen_at, boot}`. A process with no in-memory observation resumes it when it is safe:
- same boot id (`/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id`; macOS `kern.bootsessionuuid`): monotonic time is shared by every
  process of one boot and stops in sleep (Linux CLOCK_MONOTONIC, macOS), so a resumed clock still never counts a
  Mac's sleep; no boot id -> no resume (old behaviour);
- `since <= seen_at <= now` (no clock from the future);
- last observed within REPLICA_STALE_S: a longer unwatched span (gateway down, sync off) says nothing about the
  replica, so the clock starts afresh instead of alarming at once.
A detached/unsynced board drops its record, so a later attach starts afresh. The one-card-per-incident path is
unchanged; the persisted `open` flag keeps a restarted process from filing the same incident again.

Also pins two mutants that survived the post-merge check (t_01a1d5c30d953d84):
- A7 `_mode(path) not in ("primary",)`: shadow-mode boards are judged too (test_a_shadow_mode_board_is_judged_too);
- A9 `note_round` dropped from `outbox_age.after_round`: the card's last-round text comes through the loop's own
  call (test_the_sync_loops_after_round_records_the_outcome_the_card_names).
Both new tests fail with their mutant applied (2 failed, 24 passed) and pass without it.

RED on main (b4e84e04ce): test_a_stall_across_gateway_restarts_every_4_min_files_exactly_one_card and
test_restarts_resume_the_awake_clock_but_never_count_sleep fail `assert 0 == 1` (no card ever filed).
GREEN: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_replica_age.py 26 passed (test_sleep_never_counts included);
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync*.py 54 files, 1422 tests passed.

Card: t_01a1d5ead18cf1c3
